Findings
--------
1. Exposed configuration file over HTTP
   Severity: High
   Evidence file: vapt_va_evidence.txt
   Fix: Remove config.env (or any secret) from any web-served directory;
        store credentials in environment variables or a secrets manager,
        never in a world-readable served folder.

2. Credential reuse enabling SSH access
   Severity: High
   Evidence file: vapt_pt_evidence.txt
   Fix: Rotate the bpo_app password immediately since it was exposed;
        enforce unique, non-shared credentials between app config and
        OS-level accounts; consider key-based SSH auth instead of
        passwords.

